#: ../../source/hermes-agent_SKILL.md:14
msgid "Hermes Agent"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-agent_SKILL.md:16
msgid ""
"Hermes Agent is an open-source AI agent framework by Nous Research that "
"runs in your terminal, messaging platforms, and IDEs. It belongs to the "
"same category as Claude Code (Anthropic), Codex (OpenAI), and OpenClaw — "
"autonomous coding and task-execution agents that use tool calling to "
"interact with your system. Hermes works with any LLM provider "
"(OpenRouter, Anthropic, OpenAI, DeepSeek, local models, and 15+ others) "
"and runs on Linux, macOS, and WSL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-agent_SKILL.md:18
msgid "What makes Hermes different:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-agent_SKILL.md:20
msgid ""
"**Self-improving through skills** — Hermes learns from experience by "
"saving reusable procedures as skills. When it solves a complex problem, "
"discovers a workflow, or gets corrected, it can persist that knowledge as"
" a skill document that loads into future sessions. Skills accumulate over"
" time, making the agent better at your specific tasks and environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-agent_SKILL.md:21
msgid ""
"**Persistent memory across sessions** — remembers who you are, your "
"preferences, environment details, and lessons learned. Pluggable memory "
"backends (built-in, Honcho, Mem0, and more) let you choose how memory "
"works."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-agent_SKILL.md:22
msgid ""
"**Multi-platform gateway** — the same agent runs on Telegram, Discord, "
"Slack, WhatsApp, Signal, Matrix, Email, and 8+ other platforms with full "
"tool access, not just chat."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-agent_SKILL.md:23
msgid ""
"**Provider-agnostic** — swap models and providers mid-workflow without "
"changing anything else. Credential pools rotate across multiple API keys "
"automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-agent_SKILL.md:24
msgid ""
"**Profiles** — run multiple independent Hermes instances with isolated "
"configs, sessions, skills, and memory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-agent_SKILL.md:25
msgid ""
"**Extensible** — plugins, MCP servers, custom tools, webhook triggers, "
"cron scheduling, and the full Python ecosystem."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-agent_SKILL.md:27
msgid ""
"People use Hermes for software development, research, system "
"administration, data analysis, content creation, home automation, and "
"anything else that benefits from an AI agent with persistent context and "
"full system access."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-agent_SKILL.md:29
msgid ""
"**This skill helps you work with Hermes Agent effectively** — setting it "
"up, configuring features, spawning additional agent instances, "
"troubleshooting issues, finding the right commands and settings, and "
"understanding how the system works when you need to extend or contribute "
"to it."
msgstr ""

